  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection, Training and Medical and Psychosocial Support for Human Rights Defenders</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This three-year project seeks to continue to provide a national comprehensive medical and psychosocial support service to Human Rights Defenders throughout Zimbabwe, through a network of trained health practitioners and ancillary services. The project is based on six outputs, namely: Output 1: Violations against HRDs identified and documented in medico-legal affidavits as needed. Output 2: 90 HRDs per month who are OVT victims receive medical treatment (3240 HRDs in total) Output 3: 90 HRDs per month who are OVT victims receive counselling, including follow up sessions as needed (3240 HRDs in total) Output 4: 210 HRDs trained, over 10 initial trainings and 10 refresher trainings, in safe referral pathways, self and community safety, legal redress processes and basic medical first aid, Psychological Trauma, Psychological first aid and other basic supportive skills deemed necessary by the team. HRDs will receive protection packs to take into their communities. Output 5: 90 HRDs per month receive legal consultations and trainings (3240 HRDs in total) Output 6: 60 HRDs facing protection and safety concerns get relocation assistance as needed. The long-term envisaged impact is that HRDs who are victims of organized violence and torture (OVT) are fully rehabilitated through holistic support and empowered to fully participate and be reintegrated into society.</narrative>
  </description>
